# A spanning tree for the literal finite line triples

Every noninitial triple is a signed Parrott generator translate of an earlier
triple. The data also supplies an inverse to its packed three-point key. The
separate kernel checks certify both statements; the producer is untrusted.
This requires no new presentation enumeration or group order assumption.
Source: Parrott (1972), p.683, and Aschbacher–Smith J.5.6, printed p.447.
-/

